# Treat JavaScript sources as text when diffing, whatever bytes they contain.
#
# Git guesses binary-vs-text by sniffing for a NUL in the first few KB, so one
# control character in a string literal is enough to turn a source file into
# "Binary files differ" in every diff and pull request — and to hide it from
# `git grep`. That happened to scripts/check-issues-missing-template.mjs, a
# deploy gate, which is exactly the kind of file that most needs reviewing.
#
# `diff` only overrides that guess. It is deliberately not `text`, which would
# also turn on end-of-line normalisation and rewrite every file on checkout.
*.mjs diff
*.js  diff
*.cjs diff
